living in this flat feels  terrifying i'm spending every single  waking moment  worrying that i'm either going to burn  to death in my bed at night  or that i could lose everything that  i've worked and saved so hard for it's  just not fair  this is natasha her block of flats in  manchester  is such a fire risk residents have to  pay for a 24-hour watch  it's not just the cladding that's a fire  risk here it's the insulation in the  walls  the decking and balconies you know  essentially i'm living  in a flammable prison you know it feels  like i've had every option taken from me  through no fault of my own and you know  i want to move on and start a family  and have children i can't morally bring  them up in this flat when i know that  it's a fire risk  to remove the cladding alone would cost  each resident  38 000 pounds the government has long  promised help  and today residents found out what was  on offer  further funding available to pay for the  removal and replacement  of unsafe cladding for all leaseholders  in high-rise  residential buildings of 18 meters and  above  or above six stories in england  we continue to take a safety led  approach  so what does that mean for people like  natasha well because her block is 19  meters tall she will be able to get a  grant to remove cladding  but she'll have to pay for all other  works the fire wardens and insurance  which costs  thousands but she is still better off  than charlotte who lives in a nearby  block  her building is 15 meters high that  means  no grant but a loan for cladding and  like natasha  no money to cover additional costs  everything i have is in this property  at the moment it's worth zero pounds so  all of that money that i invested  into a property is effectively at the  moment worth  nothing and i'm a little bit worried  that the cost of the actual remediation  could end up being more than the deposit  on the flight in the first place  which begs the question of what was  actually the point in 